# __PROJECT_NAME__

A Go API laid out as a modular monolith: hexagonal feature modules on a shared
platform, with layer rules enforced by go-arch-lint. Generated by hexgen.

## Prerequisites

- Go 1.27 or later
- Docker and Docker Compose (Postgres, Redis, and the test containers)
- Make

## Quick Start

```bash
make setup            # dev tooling, and .env from .env.example
make docker-up        # start postgres and redis
make migrate-install  # goose and river CLIs
make migrate-up       # apply db/migrations
make run              # API on :8080
curl localhost:8080/health
```

Run `make migrate-jobs` too once a module enqueues River jobs.

## Project Structure

```text
cmd/api/            API entry point
internal/app/       composition root: builds every feature Service and wires their ports
internal/server/    HTTP server and router; every route is mounted in router.go
internal/config/    infrastructure env config
internal/platform/  infrastructure with no feature knowledge (database, cache, jobqueue, web, ...)
internal/testutil/  shared Postgres and Redis test containers
db/migrations/      goose migrations
```

## Adding a Feature Module

1. Create `internal/features/<name>/` with `service.go`, `repository.go`,
   `domain/`, and the adapters it needs under `adapter/` (`postgres/`, `http/`).
2. Build it in `internal/app/app.go` and add a field for it on `Services`.
3. Mount its routes on the `api` group in `internal/server/router.go`.
4. Add `ft-<name>`, `ft-<name>-domain` and `ft-<name>-adapter` to the
   components and deps in `.go-arch-lint.yml`, then run `make check-arch`.
5. Add its migration with `make migrate-create name=create_<name>s`.

`hexgen feature <name>` will automate these steps.

## Common Commands

```bash
make test        # all tests (requires Docker)
make lint        # golangci-lint
make check-arch  # layer rules
make mocks       # regenerate mockery mocks
make test-clean  # remove this project's test containers
make help        # every target
```
